## [ENT-064] | 2026-11-16 21:28 UTC | Unity | error | ref: game/fleet/routes.py | see: orders.log ENT-018
Class: money that only changed hands or was booked by a constant, read as earned or lost (three faults of one evening, all in the fleet's money figures).
Case 1: the birth script booked the survey mission of every pilot born this evening as 20,000 cr paid once; the game paid 4,000 (its own line in the birth log). 95 rows stood 16,000 cr too high and 3 paid pilots had no row.
Effect 1: the fleet's steady money of the last hour read -1,530,341 cr at 20:54 UTC; the money booked once was 1,508,000 cr too high.
Case 2: the wallet guard gave the new ships about 15,000 to 19,000 cr each out of ships on standing work. A pass that met a gate timeout ended in a fault after it had given and booked nothing (19:55 to 21:04 UTC). And no run's figure knew of a gift at all: every run counts its pilot's wallet from start to end.
Effect 2: the givers' routes read a loss of 1,700 to 2,300 cr a ship-hour (three gather routes), the forecast -298,508 cr an hour for the fleet at 20:54 UTC, and the takers' first routes a gain nobody made. Orders ENT-018 were written before these figures were read; they quote none of them.
Case 3: my first fix took a gift out of every run whose span held it. The spans of two runs in a row overlap by seven minutes, so a gift near the seam was taken out of both, and the second run read +19,000 cr: one gather route read +292 cr a ship-hour for ten minutes (21:18 to 21:28 UTC).
Cause: one-time money booked from a constant in a script and not from the game's answer; a record written at the end of a pass and not with each gift; a figure built on a wallet's change with no record of what else moves a wallet.
Fix: birth.py books what the game's answer names. Commit 92f6796: routes.earned and the dispatcher's loss stop leave the guard's gifts out (routes.moved); wallet.py books each gift the moment the game took it, and a gate that does not answer ends no pass; store.py recount. Commit 5044add: one gift counts in one run, well inside it or, near a seam, where that run's wallet shows it. The record was mended by hand: 95 survey rows set to 4,000 and 3 added; 55 gift rows reconstructed from the runs that show them (25 givers, 485,000 cr; 30 takers, 521,251 cr; each marked `reconstructed`, known to about a hundred credits). After it, at 21:28 UTC: the fleet's last hour +1,767 cr, the forecast -22,919 cr an hour, the gather routes -136 and -190 cr a ship-hour.
Would the fix have prevented it: case 1 and case 2 yes (tests fail on the old code); case 3 is the test added with 5044add.
Not done: the weekly tax is taken out of a run by the same overlapping span (taxes.in_run) and can count in two runs at the next assessment; three circuit runs that gave (about 47,000 cr) are not mended, because a circuit may buy and its row does not say what; why the survey paid 4,000 cr this evening and 20,000 before is not known.

